-- Help Center: the Event Partner plan (owner decision 2026-11-09). INSERT OR IGNORE, so an article edited in Admin is never overwritten. No prices in the article: they are on /pricing.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO help_articles (slug, title, category, kind, summary, body, keywords, video, sort, status, updated_by) VALUES ('event-partner-plan', 'Event Partner for cities, chambers and nonprofits', 'post', 'howto', 'Listing an event is free. Event Partner is an optional plan for organizations with several events: one payment per season covers up to 10 events with the Featured pin and an Event Partner badge.', 'Listing an event on SoCal Lights is free for everyone, and it stays free. **Event Partner** is an optional plan for cities, chambers of commerce, nonprofits and event producers that run several events in a season. The [Pricing page](/pricing#events) shows the price.

## What you get
- One payment for the season covers up to 10 of your organization''s events in that season.
- Each covered event gets the **Featured pin**: a gold-ringed pin on the map and a "Featured" badge in the list and in its details.
- Featuring opens 30 days before an event starts. It runs from the day you use the plan on the event to the event''s last day, or to the end of the season, whichever comes first. The Christmas lights season ends on January 6.
- Each covered event shows an **Event Partner** badge on its page. The badge only shows that the organization has this plan. It is not an endorsement by SoCal Lights. When the organizer''s email is at the organization''s own website, the page also says "Verified email domain".

## How to use it
1. Open [Event Partner](/partner) and sign in with the email you use for your organization. If it is at your organization''s own website, it is matched to the organization automatically.
2. Pay once on Stripe''s secure page. Stripe emails your receipt and we send a short confirmation.
3. On the same page, choose **Use the plan** next to each of your events. The page shows how many of the 10 events you have used.

You need an event on your account first: [add it for free](/add-event), or claim a listing that is already on the map. Cancelled or postponed events cannot be featured, and an event that already has the Featured pin for its whole run does not need one of your 10.

## Founding cities
Founding city partners have Event Partner free through the end of 2026. They see no price and nothing to pay.

## Refunds
If we cannot apply what you paid for, you get a full refund. A refund or a chargeback switches off the Featured pins the plan applied, so email info@socallights.app before disputing a charge. See the [Terms](/terms#paid) and [Feature an event or a home](/help/feature-an-event-or-home).', 'event partner city chamber nonprofit producer organization several events season plan badge featured pin ten events founding city', '', 55, 'published', 'seed');
